  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post-Flood Housing Reconstruction Pilot in Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022, Pakistan endured severe monsoon weather, which saw area weighted rainfall 67 per cent above normal levels in June alone. The floods affected 33 million people and caused severe damage to over two million houses. Sindh was the most affected province, with 49 per cent of the population directly affected. The catastrophic floods are a wake-up call for systemic changes to address the underlying vulnerabilities to natural hazards and their intersection with other shocks in Pakistan, calling for urgent responses and assistance delivered in an efficient, equitable, and transparent manner. 
 
Through this project, IOM aims to implement an integrated Shelter, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), and Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) pilot intervention in South Sindh, assisting communities affected by the 2022 floods to strengthen community infrastructure (including WASH infrastructure) and rebuild their houses.</narrative>
  </description>
